\\\",\\\"why_it_is_the_biggest\\\":\\\"It is the most severe and cross-border developing story surfaced across the feeds: a deadly outbreak with confirmed fatalities, hundreds of suspected cases, regional spread risk, and additional international exposure concerns.\\\"},\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Multiple feeds converged on an Ebola outbreak in the DRC’s Ituri province. The Guardian reported 65 deaths and 246 suspected cases, while BBC highlighted additional exposure concerns involving Americans. The outbreak is especially worrying because officials identified the Bundibugyo strain, for which there is no licensed vaccine, and neighboring Uganda has already confirmed an outbreak.\\\",\\\"key_facts\\\":[{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"65 people have died in the DRC outbreak.\\\",\\\"support\\\":[\\\"The Guardian\\\"]},{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"246 suspected cases have been reported so far, mainly in Ituri province.\\\",\\\"support\\\":[\\\"The Guardian\\\"]},{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"Cases are concentrated in the Mongwalu and Rwampara health zones, with suspected cases also in Bunia.\\\",\\\"support\\\":[\\\"The Guardian\\\"]},{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"Uganda confirmed an outbreak and a 59-year-old man died in a Kampala hospital after traveling from the DRC.\\\",\\\"support\\\":[\\\"The Guardian\\\"]},{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"DRC health officials said 13 of 20 tested samples were positive for Ebola virus.\\\",\\\"support\\\":[\\\"The Guardian\\\"]},{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"The strain identified was Bundibugyo, for which there is no licensed vaccine.\\\",\\\"support\\\":[\\\"The Guardian\\\"]},{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"BBC reported at least six Americans were exposed during the DRC outbreak, with one reportedly symptomatic.\\\",\\\"support\\\":[\\\"BBC News\\\"]},{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"The outbreak is complicated by high population movement through mining towns and border regions.\\\",\\\"support\\\":[\\\"The Guardian\\\"]},{\\\"fact\\\":\\\"Africa CDC said rapid regional coordination is essential and convened an urgent meeting with DRC, U