{"type":"message","id":"81c243a3","parentId":"ccde091d","timestamp":"2026-05-18T10:56:42.193Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5PocHePenm33j9kvTNUGMEQK","toolName":"memory_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2285923d57b28a4ede63d1e5e1c171d55ba73cdab477c0fc561036eea2acdf07\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 1226,\n      \"endLine\": 1283,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.507416887433657,\n      \"snippet\": \"assistant: [[reply_to_current]] Absolutely — here’s a **developer checklist** for fixing the continuous-run behavior.\\n\\n# Developer Checklist — Continuous Crypto Pipeline\\n\\n## A. Workflow ownership\\n- [ ] Define the pipeline as **one active workflow**, not a series of unrelated chat replies\\n- [ ] Ensure one component clearly owns the run from **Step 0 through Step 5**\\n- [ ] Ensure Step 6 is only triggered from explicit user confirmation\\n- [ ] Prevent chat-turn boundaries from acting like implicit stop points\\n\\n---\\n\\n## B. State machine\\n- [ ] Add explicit run status values:\\n  - [ ] `idle`\\n  - [ ] `active`\\n  - [ ] `awaiting_user_confirmation`\\n  - [ ] `blocked_approval`\\n  - [ ] `blocked_error`\\n  - [\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1226-L1283\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1226-L1283\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"323ca4090dd3a4e98ce45390d41d023585cda64c88319ba290c2cf3021f63075\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 612,\n      \"endLine\": 701,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.5519904660743369,\n      \"snippet\": \"- required artifact missing after retry policy exhausted\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 6) Step-by-step execution contract\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Step 0 — Initialize Run\\n\\n### Entry condition\\nUser sends:\\n- “run pipeline”\\n- “run crypto news pipeline”\\n- “start crypto pipeline”\\n\\n### Required actions\\n- generate run id and run dir\\n- create symlinks\\n- initialize manifest\\n- set:\\n  - `status=active`\\n  - `current_step=init`\\n  - `next_step=research`\\n\\n### Exit condition\\nManifest exists and init is marked succeeded.\\n\\n### Next action\\nImmediately start Step 1.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Step 1 — Research\\n\\n### Entry condition\\n- `current_step=research`\\n- `steps.research.status=pending|retrying`\\n\\n### Required actions\\n- clear researcher session file\\n- run research\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L612-L701\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L612-L701\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"154612d0b595f1c47938949a1a204576d95aae66d5982419c45fe3b5295699d9\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 748,\n      \"endLine\": 821,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.721743468291449,\n      \"snippet\": \"- strip chart placeholders from export path or mark expected placeholders = 0 according to current pipeline design\\n- mark step as `skipped_with_warning` or `failed_nonblocking`\\n\\n### On success\\n- manifest update\\n- `next_step=generate_image`\\n\\n### Required behavior\\nImmediately continue to image step.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Step 3 — Generate Feature Image\\n\\n### Entry condition\\n- chart step resolved, success or nonblocking skip\\n\\n### Required actions\\n- clear creator session file\\n- run creator agent\\n- validate output image if present\\n\\n### Failure handling\\nFeature image failure is nonblocking.\\n\\n### On success or nonblocking skip\\n- manifest update\\n- `next_step=publish_drive`\\n\\n### Required behavior\\nImmediately conti\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L748-L821\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L748-L821\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d7064ae23a164816a1ce278ef13567be76f9df06965ce06f462e3460fc85e3bb\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 209,\n      \"endLine\": 264,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.6743224650353566,\n      \"snippet\": \"**Problem:**  \\nThe pipeline spans multiple long steps:\\n- research\\n- writing\\n- chart\\n- image\\n- drive publish\\n- optional wordpress publish\\n\\nThat is bigger than a fragile step-by-step chat reply chain.\\n\\n**Fix needed:**  \\nUse one durable execution owner for the whole run.\\n\\n### Best design options\\n\\n#### Option A — Best recommendation\\nRun the full pipeline inside **one durable background workflow** that owns Steps 0–5 end-to-end, and only message you at meaningful milestones.\\n\\nWhy this is best:\\n- avoids chat-turn fragmentation\\n- avoids accidental stopping after status messages\\n- easier resume/recovery\\n- clearer single source of truth\\n\\n#### Option B — Acceptable\\nKeep the current chat orchestration\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L209-L264\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L209-L264\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e8df757c55657f3db361e35b7f0ebac421b66ede22cfb34ae11f75477fe135b4\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 86,\n      \"endLine\": 135,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.6655886518438168,\n      \"snippet\": \"of silently continuing\\\\n\\\\nIf you want, I can patch the pipeline so future Google Docs include the chart correctly.\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\nno you do not do anything just let me know what to fix\\nassistant: [[reply_to_current]] Yep — here’s **exactly what needs fixing**, nothing more:\\n\\n### 1) Fix the chart generator\\nThe chart step is producing something that is **not a real PNG**.\\n\\nWhat to fix:\\n- Make sure the chart agent writes a **valid PNG binary** to:\\n  - `/tmp/chart.png`\\n- Make sure it does **not** write text/log output into the chart file\\n- Make sure the generator respects:\\n  - `CHART_OUTPUT: /tmp/chart.png`\\n\\n### 2) Fix the DOCX export step\\nRight now the export only prepends the feature image and never\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md#L86-L135\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-chart-fix.md#L86-L135\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"provider\": \"none\",\n  \"citations\": \"auto\",\n  \"debug\": {\n    \"backend\": \"builtin\",\n    \"effectiveMode\": \"n/a\",\n    \"searchMs\": 47,\n    \"hits\": 5\n  }\n}"}],"details":{"results":[{"id":"2285923d57b28a4ede63d1e5e1c171d55ba73cdab477c0fc561036eea2acdf07","path":"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md","startLine":1226,"endLine":1283,"score":1,"textScore":0.507416887433657,"snippet":"assistant: [[reply_to_current]] Absolutely — here’s a **developer checklist** for fixing the continuous-run behavior.\n\n# Developer Checklist — Continuous Crypto Pipeline\n\n## A. Workflow ownership\n- [ ] Define the pipeline as **one active workflow**, not a series of unrelated chat replies\n- [ ] Ensure one component clearly owns the run from **Step 0 through Step 5**\n- [ ] Ensure Step 6 is only triggered from explicit user confirmation\n- [ ] Prevent chat-turn boundaries from acting like implicit stop points\n\n---\n\n## B. State machine\n- [ ] Add explicit run status values:\n  - [ ] `idle`\n  - [ ] `active`\n  - [ ] `awaiting_user_confirmation`\n  - [ ] `blocked_approval`\n  - [ ] `blocked_error`\n  - [\n\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1226-L1283","source":"memory","citation":"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1226-L1283","corpus":"memory"},{"id":"323ca4090dd3a4e98ce45390d41d023585cda64c88319ba290c2cf3021f63075","path":"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md","startLine":612,"endLine":701,"score":1,"textScore":0.5519904660743369,"snippet":"- required artifact missing after retry policy exhausted