{"type":"message","id":"2c22d63b","parentId":"c0e492fa","timestamp":"2026-05-18T11:01:48.458Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Chart fix worked ✅\n\n- retest passed\n- real file is a valid PNG\n- size: `64014 bytes`\n\nImage is interesting: the **agent still reported failure**, but the actual file on disk now looks valid too.\n\nI checked the real image target and got:\n- exists: yes\n- size: `296584 bytes`\n- type: `JPEG image data`\n- resolution: `1024x576`\n\nSo the current state is:\n\n### Chart\n- **fixed**\n- validator now works correctly\n\n### Image\n- the **generated image file is valid**\n- but the **creator agent is still falsely reporting failure**\n- that means the remaining bug is probably in the creator’s **success/failure detection or final status reporting**, not the actual image generation output\n\n### Simple resolution for image\nYour developer should check the creator flow for this pattern:\n- image download/save succeeds\n- final file is valid\n- but some intermediate check still sees the old `43 bytes` temp/error response\n- or the agent raises failure before/after the final good file is written\n\nMost likely fixes:\n1. validate the **final output path** before declaring failure\n2. don’t return `IMAGE_FAILED` if `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` ends up being a valid JPEG over the minimum size\n3. make sure temp download errors don’t override a later successful save\n\nSo short answer:\n- **chart issue is fixed**\n- **image generation itself seems fixed too**\n- **remaining bug is false failure reporting in creator**\n\nIf you want, I can give you a very small exact rule your developer can add:\n> “If final output exists and passes JPEG + size validation, return success even if an earlier download attempt failed.”"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":248,"output":357,"cacheRead":49920,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":50525,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"c